### Interface styles (3.8.0) ###
OblyonDensity                  = Interface density
OblyonDensityHelp              = Height of the table rows and headers, of the input fields, of the action buttons and inner margins of the cards
OblyonDensityCompact           = Compact (original rendering)
OblyonDensityNormal            = Normal
OblyonDensityComfortable       = Comfortable
OblyonTabsStyle                = Style of the card tabs
OblyonTabsStyleHelp            = Boxed: framed tabs standing on the card (original rendering). Underlined: flat tabs on a rule, the active one is underlined with the main colour. Pills: rounded tabs, the active one on a background tinted with the main colour
OblyonTabsStyleBoxed           = Boxed (original rendering)
OblyonTabsStyleUnderline       = Underlined
OblyonTabsStylePills           = Pills
OblyonTabPillBorder            = Pill tabs: border (colour in the Colors tab, Tabs group)
OblyonTabPillShadow            = Pill tabs: drop shadow
OblyonButtonStyle              = Style of the action buttons
OblyonButtonStyleHelp          = Applies to the action buttons of the cards, to the Delete button and to the form buttons (Save, Cancel...). Filled: coloured background (original rendering). Outline: transparent background, coloured frame and text. Soft: lightly tinted background, coloured text. The colours of each family (background, text, border, hover) are set in the Colors tab, Buttons group
OblyonButtonStyleFilled        = Filled (original rendering)
OblyonButtonStyleOutline       = Outline
OblyonButtonStyleSoft          = Soft
OblyonButtonFormOwnColors      = Own colours for the form buttons
OblyonButtonFormOwnColorsHelp  = By default the form buttons (Save, Cancel, Search...) take the colours of the action buttons. Enable to give them their own colours (new family in the Colors tab, Buttons group)
OblyonBtnGroupHelp             = Current button style: %s (Options tab). The colours shown are the ones really applied. A colour you do not change stays automatic: it follows the button style and the base colours; a changed colour is kept as is
OblyonBtnFamilyAction          = Action buttons (Modify, Validate, Send...)
OblyonBtnFamilyDelete          = Delete button
OblyonBtnFamilyForm            = Form buttons (Save, Cancel, Search...)
OblyonBtnRoleBg                = Background
OblyonBtnRoleTxt               = Text
OblyonBtnRoleBorder            = Border
OblyonBtnRoleBgHover           = Hover background
OblyonBtnRoleTxtHover          = Hover text
OblyonBadgeStyle               = Display of the statuses
OblyonBadgeStyleHelp           = Icon: image dot of the core, without label. Filled pill: badge with the status colour as background (original rendering). Outline: badge on the row background, frame and text of the status colour. Dot + text: a disc of the status colour before the label, no background nor frame (lighter lists). The badge colours are set in the Colors tab, Status badges group
OblyonBadgeStyleIcon           = Icon (image dot)
OblyonBadgeStylePill           = Filled pill badge (original rendering)
OblyonBadgeStyleOutline        = Outline badge
OblyonBadgeStyleDot            = Dot + text
OblyonStatusPulse              = Pulse of the status of the open card
OblyonStatusPulseHelp          = The status shown in the card banner (right of the reference) softly fades from full opacity to 55 %% and back over 2.4 seconds, in its own colour, without resizing; paused on hover for reading. Never in the lists. With the "Dot + text" style only the disc pulses
OblyonListHeaderStyle          = Style of the list headers
OblyonListHeaderStyleHelp      = Coloured band: title row and filter row on the title background (original rendering). Flat: title on the row background, muted text closed by a rule, sorted column in the main colour, filters on a barely tinted background, matching "like the header" totals. The colours of the flat style are set in the Colors tab, Titles group. The dashboard widget titles do not change
OblyonListHeaderStyleBand      = Coloured band (original rendering)
OblyonListHeaderStyleFlat      = Flat
OblyonMotion                   = Animations
OblyonMotionHelp               = Applies to every transition and animation of the theme: menus and flyouts, mobile drawer, buttons, tabs, dashboard tiles, status pulse. Normal: theme animations, unless the device asks for reduced motion (Windows "Animation effects", macOS "Reduce motion", phones), in which case they are reduced automatically. Reduced: transitions cut to 50 ms and animations disabled for everybody
OblyonMotionNormal             = Normal (reduced when the device asks for it)
OblyonMotionReduced            = Reduced
OblyonNotifCenter              = Notification center
OblyonNotifCenterHelp          = Shows a bell at the top right, next to the user block. Every Dolibarr message (confirmation, warning, error) is shown briefly as today, then stays available in the bell, with a badge of the unread count. Errors and warnings are no longer displayed permanently: 6 seconds, then the bell. History kept in the user's browser (50 messages, 7 days), nothing in the database
OblyonNotifTitle               = Notifications
OblyonNotifEmpty               = No notification
OblyonNotifMarkRead            = Mark all as read
OblyonNotifClear               = Clear all
OblyonNotifDelete              = Delete this notification
OblyonNotifNow                 = just now
OblyonNotifMin                 = %s min ago
OblyonNotifHour                = %s h ago
OblyonNotifDay                 = %s d ago
OblyonUserBlock                = User block (top bar)
OblyonUserBlockHelp            = Default: the user's photo or a generic silhouette, original dropdown menu. Initials: a circle of the main colour carrying the user's initials (first name + last name, else login) instead of the photo, in the bar and in the dropdown. Photo: the user's photo when set, else the initials. With Initials or Photo, the user dropdown is redesigned: floating card, centred header on the accent tint, "Show..." links as clickable rows, Card and Logout buttons in the theme button colours
OblyonUserBlockDefault         = Default (original rendering)
OblyonUserBlockInitials        = Initials
OblyonUserBlockPhoto           = Photo, else initials
OblyonAgendaStyle              = Agenda style
OblyonAgendaStyleHelp          = Month, week and day views of the native agenda. Classic: original rendering. Modern: days of the month on the row background, other days muted, today on the accent tint with the number in a disc of the main colour, "+" button shown on hover, flat day header, every event as a card tinted with its own colour (type or user) with readable text. Third-party agenda modules (FullCalendar...) are not affected
OblyonAgendaStyleClassic       = Classic (original rendering)
OblyonAgendaStyleModern        = Modern
### TakePOS (3.9.0) ###
OblyonTakepos                   = Point of sale (TakePOS)
OblyonTakeposTitle              = TakePOS point of sale interface
OblyonTakeposTheme              = Point of sale theme
OblyonTakeposThemeHelp          = Applies to every terminal. Native: original TakePOS rendering. Enhanced native: original layout, more readable (big spaced buttons, large total, visible selected line, highlighted Payment button). Counter: categories as tabs, large product grid, ticket on the right with the payment bar, numeric pad as a panel on demand. Tablet: grid of the categories then of the products, ticket, numeric pad always visible and payment on the right. Grocery store: large scan field, wide ticket table, payment and keyboard shortcut help on the right, categories and products as a band. Every theme except Native adds the -/+ buttons on the lines, the quick discounts and the keyboard shortcuts. Reload the point of sale (Ctrl+F5) after a change
OblyonTakeposThemeNative        = Native (original TakePOS rendering)
OblyonTakeposThemeClassic       = Enhanced native
OblyonTakeposThemeCounter       = Counter
OblyonTakeposThemeTablet        = Tablet
OblyonTakeposThemeScanner       = Grocery store (scan and keyboard)
OblyonTakeposQuickDiscounts     = Quick discounts (in %%, comma separated)
OblyonTakeposQuickDiscountsHelp = One-tap discount buttons of the payment bar (Counter, Tablet, Grocery store): applied to the selected line, else to the last line of the ticket. Up to 4 values between 0 and 100, for example 5,10,20; 0 removes the discount. The minimum price of the products is still checked by TakePOS
OblyonTakeposAutoNewSale        = Automatic new sale after the payment (seconds, 0 = never)
OblyonTakeposAutoNewSaleHelp    = Counter, Tablet and Grocery store themes: after a payment, the bar shows "Sale completed", the print buttons of the paid ticket and a New sale button (or F9); at the end of the delay, the next sale starts by itself. Adding an item also starts the next sale. The reprint buttons stay available until the first item. 0: the next sale only starts on click
OblyonTakeposCategoryColors     = Category colours on the tiles
OblyonTakeposCategoryColorsHelp = Every category tile takes the colour of its Dolibarr category (Colour field of the category card): frame and label band, or the whole tab in the Counter and Grocery store themes. Product tiles carry a stripe of the colour of the displayed category (not during a search). A category without colour keeps the theme rendering. Works with every point of sale theme
OblyonTakeposColorfulWarning    = The "Colorful" theme of the TakePOS module is enabled: its colours are replaced by the ones of the theme chosen here
OblyonTakeposReactivateWarning  = The -/+ buttons of the ticket lines require to disable then enable the Oblyon module once (new hook of the ticket). The rest of the theme already works
OblyonTakeposSetupLink          = Other display settings of the point of sale (TakePOS module)
OblyonTakeposModuleDisabled     = The Point of sale (TakePOS) module is not enabled: no point of sale setting is available
OblyonTakeposNumpad             = Numeric pad
OblyonTakeposClose              = Close
OblyonTakeposBack               = Categories
OblyonTakeposKeys               = Keyboard shortcuts
OblyonTakeposKeyLines           = Previous / next line
OblyonTakeposKeyStep            = Quantity -1 / +1
OblyonTakeposKeyNumberHint      = Type a number in the search field then Alt+Q, Alt+R or Alt+P: it becomes the quantity, the discount or the price of the selected line
OblyonTakeposQtyMinus           = Remove one item
OblyonTakeposQtyPlus            = Add one item
OblyonTakeposQtyDelete          = Delete the line
OblyonTakeposSaleDone           = Sale completed
OblyonTakeposNewSale            = New sale
